    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0450" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">391.1163 Lutheran Orient Mission/95:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merriam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-24T12:00:00+03:25">March 24,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Lutheran missionaries at Saujbulak in Azerbaijan have been ordered to leave
                    by the local governor. This morning I asked the acting Foreign Minister to delay
                    action pending full investigation and drew his attention to the exchange of
                    notes dated May 14, 1928,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d475-f1"/> relating to
                    missionary activities.</p>
                <p>He did not mention <hi rendition="#italic">Mirror</hi> article<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d475-f2"/> during our friendly interview and of course I refrained
                    from doing so.</p>
                <p>He said that Anayat Ollah Sami’i heretofore Iranian Minister at Baghdad has been
                    appointed Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merriam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d475-f1" n="22" xml:id="d475-f1-content">
                <p>For text of notes, see <ref target="frus1928v03#pg_724"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, 1928, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >iii</hi>, p. 724</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d475-f2" n="23" xml:id="d475-f2-content">
                <p>The article in the New York <hi rendition="#italic">Daily Mirror</hi> which led
                    to the withdrawal of the Iranian representatives in the United States. See
                    memorandum by the Under Secretary of State, March 14, and following
                    correspondence, <ref target="#pg350">pp. 350</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
